# bhumi (भूमि — "ground / earth") — sovereign userland platform backend
# for the AGNOS compositor (aethersafha).
#
# WHAT bhumi OWNS
# --------------
# bhumi is the userland layer that sits BETWEEN aethersafha and the agnos
# kernel — the sovereign replacement for the Linux compositor-backend trio
# (DRM/KMS + libinput + logind). It is NOT XWayland and NOT a client-compat
# bridge (that is `mehman`). bhumi is a *platform* backend: it gives the
# compositor pixels-out, events-in, and a seat — nothing about clients.
#
#   Linux backend            →  bhumi module          →  agnos surface
#   ------------------------    --------------------     ----------------------
#   DRM/KMS (libdrm)         →  src/output.cyr        →  agnodrm → kernel blit#39 / FB
#   libinput / evdev         →  src/input.cyr         →  kernel hid_poll input events
#   logind session/seat      →  src/seat.cyr          →  native seat (sigil/kavach gate)
#   (assembled backend)      →  src/backend.cyr       →  the handle aethersafha instantiates
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT HERE
# ---------------------
# - X11 / XWayland: AGNOS has zero native X11 clients; the bug class does not exist.
# - foreign-app surface hosting: that is `mehman` (the swallow-stage compat backend).
# - the Wayland protocol / client lifecycle: that is aethersafha proper.
#
# bhumi is the FIRST of the two compositor backends to build — aethersafha
# sits directly on it. `mehman` is post-MVP.
#
# Re-exported via dist/bhumi.cyr (cyrius distlib). Domain modules land in the
# sibling files above as the M0→M-n bites land (see docs/development/roadmap.md);
# programs/smoke.cyr proves the include chain compiles end-to-end.

# --- module include chain (uncomment as each module lands) ---
include "src/output.cyr"       # pixels-out: software framebuffer (BhumiFb)
include "src/scanout.cyr"      # kernel handoff: agnos fbinfo#38 / blit#39 (cross-target)
include "src/pattern.cyr"      # bring-up test patterns (color bars, XOR) over a BhumiFb
include "src/input.cyr"        # events-in: USB HID keyboard report decode
include "src/kbscan.cyr"       # kernel drain: agnos kbscan#42 -> HID reports (cross-target)
include "src/seat.cyr"         # sovereign seat: capability-gated device access (sigil/kavach)
# include "src/backend.cyr"    # assembled platform-backend handle

# Scaffold sentinel — proves the lib header compiles before any module lands.
# Removed when src/backend.cyr lands the real public surface.
fn bhumi_scaffold_ok(): i64 { return 1; }
